    {
      "id": "59punf8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background: Rise of New Religions"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Vardhamana Mahavira was the 24th Tirthankara of Jainism, advocating strict adherence to non-violence and asceticism.",
        "Gautama Buddha attained enlightenment at Bodh Gaya and delivered his first sermon at Sarnath, known as Dharmachakra Pravartana.",
        "Buddhism core teachings center on the Four Noble Truths and the Eightfold Path (Ashtangika Marga) to achieve Nirvana.",
        "Primary literary sources include Prakrit texts for Jainism and Pali canonical literature (Tripitakas) for Buddhism."
      ],
      "id": "d1odqyd"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xohhr6p",
      "content": "• By the 6th century BCE many people were dissatisfied with the complex rituals of Vedic religion."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xa5fsum",
      "content": "• The dominance of Brahmins and rigid caste system created social tensions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ksdvulg",
      "content": "• Expensive sacrifices (Yajnas) were difficult for common people."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7fs02sh",
      "content": "• As a result, new religious movements like Jainism and Buddhism emerged."
    },
    {
      "id": "ufg2qta",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Jainism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "srx5nrr",
      "content": "Jainism is one of the oldest religions in India. It emphasizes non‑violence, self‑discipline and spiritual purity."
    },
